      "writtenOn": "2021-12-06T23:49:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have to use per-cpu lock to avoid performance regression in the hot path. Upstream folks working on SPF were concerned about cacheline-bouncing if we use rw_semaphore. I profiled per-cpu lock vs rw_semaphore during pagefaults and it shows 3x performance improvement. Upstream fix for the latest SPF that Michel will be posting will implement the same approach.",
      "parentUuid": "70b7ecf2_76c043b1",
